{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Feature Selection Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Generate synthetic data with known feature structure"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_feature_selection_data(n_samples=500, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x1 = rng.randn(n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x2 = rng.randn(n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x3 = rng.randn(n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x4 = x1 + 0.1 * rng.randn(n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x5 = x2 + 0.1 * rng.randn(n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    informative = np.column_stack([x1, x2, x3, x4, x5])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    correlated = np.column_stack(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x1 * 0.9 + 0.1 * rng.randn(n_samples),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x2 * 0.8 + 0.2 * rng.randn(n_samples),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x3 * 0.7 + 0.3 * rng.randn(n_samples),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x1 * 0.5 + x2 * 0.5 + 0.1 * rng.randn(n_samples),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x2 * 0.6 + x3 * 0.4 + 0.1 * rng.randn(n_samples),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    noise = rng.randn(n_samples, 10) * 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    X = np.hstack([informative, correlated, noise])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y = (2 * x1 - 1.5 * x2 + x3 + 0.5 * rng.randn(n_samples) > 0).astype(int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    feature_names = ("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [f\"info_{i}\" for i in range(5)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        + [f\"corr_{i}\" for i in range(5)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        + [f\"noise_{i}\" for i in range(10)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return X, y, feature_names"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We know the ground truth: features 0-4 are informative (plus 3 and 4 are correlated copies of 0 and 1), features 5-9 are correlated with informative features, features 10-19 are pure noise. A good selection method should rank 0-4 highest and 10-19 lowest."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Variance threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def variance_threshold(X, threshold=0.01):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    variances = np.var(X, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask = variances > threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mask, variances"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Mutual information (discrete)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def discretize(x, n_bins=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    min_val, max_val = x.min(), x.max()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if max_val == min_val:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return np.zeros_like(x, dtype=int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bin_edges = np.linspace(min_val, max_val, n_bins + 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    binned = np.digitize(x, bin_edges[1:-1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return binned"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mutual_information(X, y, n_bins=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_samples, n_features = X.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mi_scores = np.zeros(n_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y_vals, y_counts = np.unique(y, return_counts=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    p_y = y_counts / n_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for f in range(n_features):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_binned = discretize(X[:, f], n_bins)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_vals, x_counts = np.unique(x_binned, return_counts=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        p_x = dict(zip(x_vals, x_counts / n_samples))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mi = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for xv in x_vals:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for yi, yv in enumerate(y_vals):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                joint_mask = (x_binned == xv) & (y == yv)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                p_xy = np.sum(joint_mask) / n_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if p_xy > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    mi += p_xy * np.log(p_xy / (p_x[xv] * p_y[yi]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mi_scores[f] = mi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mi_scores"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Recursive Feature Elimination"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def simple_logistic_importance(X, y, lr=0.1, epochs=100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_samples, n_features = X.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w = np.zeros(n_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        z = X @ w + b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-np.clip(z, -500, 500)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        error = pred - y"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w -= lr * (X.T @ error) / n_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        b -= lr * np.mean(error)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return w, b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rfe(X, y, n_features_to_select=5, lr=0.1, epochs=100):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_total = X.shape[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    remaining = list(range(n_total))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rankings = np.ones(n_total, dtype=int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rank = n_total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while len(remaining) > n_features_to_select:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_subset = X[:, remaining]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w, _ = simple_logistic_importance(X_subset, y, lr, epochs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        importances = np.abs(w)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        least_idx = np.argmin(importances)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        original_idx = remaining[least_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rankings[original_idx] = rank"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rank -= 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        remaining.pop(least_idx)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for idx in remaining:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rankings[idx] = 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    selected_mask = rankings == 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return selected_mask, rankings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: L1 feature selection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def soft_threshold(w, alpha):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.sign(w) * np.maximum(np.abs(w) - alpha, 0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def l1_feature_selection(X, y, alpha=0.1, lr=0.01, epochs=500):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_samples, n_features = X.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    w = np.zeros(n_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    b = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        z = X @ w + b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-np.clip(z, -500, 500)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        error = pred - y"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gradient_w = (X.T @ error) / n_samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gradient_b = np.mean(error)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w -= lr * gradient_w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w = soft_threshold(w, lr * alpha)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        b -= lr * gradient_b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    selected_mask = np.abs(w) > 1e-6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return selected_mask, w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Tree-based importance (simple decision tree)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gini_impurity(y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if len(y) == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    classes, counts = np.unique(y, return_counts=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = counts / len(y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 - np.sum(probs ** 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def best_split(X, y, feature_idx):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    values = np.unique(X[:, feature_idx])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if len(values) <= 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return None, -1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_threshold = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_gain = -1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    parent_gini = gini_impurity(y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(len(values) - 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        threshold = (values[i] + values[i + 1]) / 2.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        left_mask = X[:, feature_idx] <= threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        right_mask = ~left_mask"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n_left = np.sum(left_mask)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n_right = np.sum(right_mask)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if n_left == 0 or n_right == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gain = parent_gini - (n_left / n) * gini_impurity(y[left_mask]) - (n_right / n) * gini_impurity(y[right_mask])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if gain > best_gain:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_gain = gain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_threshold = threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return best_threshold, best_gain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tree_importance(X, y, n_trees=50, max_depth=5, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_samples, n_features = X.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    importances = np.zeros(n_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n_trees):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sample_idx = rng.choice(n_samples, size=n_samples, replace=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        feature_subset = rng.choice(n_features, size=max(1, int(np.sqrt(n_features))), replace=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_boot = X[sample_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y_boot = y[sample_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tree_imp = _build_tree_importance(X_boot, y_boot, feature_subset, max_depth)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        importances += tree_imp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = importances.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if total > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        importances /= total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return importances"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def _build_tree_importance(X, y, feature_subset, max_depth, depth=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_features = X.shape[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    importances = np.zeros(n_features)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if depth >= max_depth or len(np.unique(y)) <= 1 or len(y) < 4:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return importances"
